From 121c56d77a8639e0522789069b29b8d40db53158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:46:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/25] Modeling Algorithms - Compute fillets of constant
 radius as rolling balls

BlendFunc_ConstRad took the center of a section of the fillet from the
normals of the surfaces projected on the plane normal to the guide: the
section was the circle tangent to the sections of the faces by that plane.
Where the normals of the faces leave that plane (a helical root, a cone off
the edge, a face inclined to the edge) this is not a ball touching the
faces. On the start wall of the FreeCAD screw thread, next to the fillet of
the root, the trace on the wall went 0.015 mm out of the one of the rolling
ball at radius 0.5, made a hook at 0.8 and a bulge instead of the corner at
1; on a quarter of a cone the fillet missed the ball by 0.22 with a radius
of 10. SolidWorks gives the rolling ball, to 0.003 mm of an independent
computation, on all these.

- BlendFunc_ConstRad and BlendFunc_ConstRadInv: the center is on the full
  normals of the surfaces, pts1 + ray1 * N1 = pts2 + ray2 * N2, the middle
  of the points of contact staying in the plane normal to the guide; the
  section is the circle of the ball in the plane through its center and
  the points of contact (its normal and derivatives replace the ones of the
  plane of the guide in the sections given to the approximation). Only the
  plane depends on the parameter of the guide now. SetRollingBall(false)
  keeps the previous section.
- ChFi3d_Builder::Compute: the ends and corners of the fillets were built
  for sections in the planes of the guides, and some of them cannot follow
  the ball (a ball which nests in a fillet of its own radius, a support
  face with a kink, a corner where the ball does not fit). When the result
  with the ball fails, is invalid or has a tolerance above 10 times the
  approximation tolerance, the contours are restored and computed again
  with the previous section, and the better result is kept.

On the screw the fillet of the wall is valid for radii 0.08-1.83 except
0.46 (0.43-0.45, 0.47 and 0.525, which failed, are built now); the full
chain of the file with FreeCAD's refine stays valid with tolerance 3.1e-4.

GTest BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.ConstantRadius_FollowsRollingBall. The tests
blend/simple/C8 and D1 (corners of a quarter of a cone) get a spherical
corner from the ball and their new areas; the tests of the screw get their
new values.

